From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: media: h713-hdmirx: the socket's port from the device tree

The driver had the HY310's socket wired in: hardware port 0 for EDID and
hot-plug (ARISC), source id 3 (HDMI-1) for SetSource and for the
SignalChange filter of the source-switch repeat. The HY320's socket is
port 1: with an Xbox One X plugged in, the display firmware's hot-plug
callback reported source 4, port 0 stayed without a signal, and HPD and
SetSource on port 1 (source 4, by the stock port map 3/4/5 -> 0/1/2
the init sequence sends) brought 1920x1080p60.

"allwinner,hdmi-port" (0..2, absent: 0) names the socket's port; the
source id follows as 3 + port. Every board without the property keeps
what it had. The log lines name the source id instead of "HDMI-1"; the
V4L2 input keeps its name. The dtsi's binding comment describes the
property.

Measured on the HY320, 01.11.2026, with the module built for port 1:
"EDID/HPD sequence on port 1 completed", the signal 1920x1080p60 and
48 kHz PCM sound (with 0336).

